  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Human Right and Environmental Due Diligence in avocado and blueberry production (FVOF22002)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Avocado and blueberry are two of the most popular fruit and vegetable products in Dutch and European households. Nature&apos;s Pride and Berries Pride are one of the biggest avocado and blueberry importers in Europe. The project partners currently don&apos;t have any real figures on the most important risks at production level, with regard to human rights and environment. Hence, this forms the rationale to further explore the selected risks deeper in the value chain for avocado and blueberry. In project A (impact assessment) partners will perform a Human Rights and Environmental Due Diligence (HREDD) for Nature&apos;s and Berries Pride operations in the field of labour conditions, water use, and greenhouse gas emissions (GHG). Through this project opportunities will be identified to reduce emissions and improve the situation together with their growers.Based on the outcomes of the impact assessment from Project A, in project B concrete mitigation plans will be implemented at for a handful of suppliers in one country.The desired outcome is to supply the European market with avocado and blueberry with &apos;next level&apos; sustainability.</narrative>
  </description>
